{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":44370322,"items":[{"DOI":"10.37418\/amsj.9.12.14","title":["KNOWING NARAYANA COWS SEQUENCE"],"author":[{"given":"R.","family":"Sivaraman","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2020,11,21]]},"container-title":["Advances in Mathematics: Scientific Journal"],"type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":1,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.37418\/amsj.9.12.14"},{"abstract":"<jats:p>Let $\\left(N_n\\right)_{n\\ge0}$ be the Narayana&amp;#39;s cows sequence and $\\left(P_n\\right)_{n\\ge0}$ the Padovan sequence, the aims in this paper is to study and completely solve the exponential Diophantine equation $N_m - P_n = N_{m_1}-N_{n_1}$ where $m, n, m_1$ and $n_1$ are\r\npositive integers with $(m, n)\\neq (m_1, n_1)$.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.5539\/jmr.v17n1p40","type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":1,"title":["Pillai&amp;#39;s Problem Involving Narayana&amp;#39;s Cows Sequence and Padovan Sequence"],"author":[{"given":"Salifou","family":"NIKIEMA","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"S\u00b4emou","family":"DIOUF","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"container-title":["Journal of Mathematics Research"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,30]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5539\/jmr.v17n1p40"},{"DOI":"10.21236\/ada198582","title":["The Atomic Structures of the Au-Induced Reconstructions of Si(111): 5 x 1, Square Root 3 x 3 Square Root 3 and 6 x 6"],"author":[{"given":"Judy H.","family":"Huang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"R. S.","family":"Williams","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[1988,7,22]]},"type":"report","is-referenced-by-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.21236\/ada198582"},{"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n        <jats:p>In recent years, the log-concavity of the $n$-th root of a sequence $\\{\\sqrt[n]{S_n}\\}_{n\\geq 1}$ has been received a lot of attention. Very recently, Sun posed the following conjecture in his new book: the sequences $\\{ \\sqrt[n]{a_n}\\}_{n\\geq 2}$ and $\\{ \\sqrt[n]{b_n}\\}_{n\\geq 1}$ are log-concave, where \\[a_n:= \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\frac{{n-1\\choose k}^2{n+k\\choose k}^2 }{4k^2-1} \\]and \\[b_n:= \\frac{1}{n^3}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} (3k^2+3k+1){n-1\\choose k}^2 {n+k\\choose k}^2. \\]In this paper, two methods, semi-automatic and analytic methods, are used to confirm Sun's conjecture. The semi-automatic method relies on a criterion on the log-concavity of $\\{\\sqrt[n]{S_n}\\}_{n\\geq 1}$ given by us and a mathematica package due to Hou and Zhang, while theanalytic method relies on a result due to Xia.\n2010 Mathematics subject classification: 05A20; 05A10.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.21203\/rs.3.rs-2352868\/v1","type":"posted-content","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["On the log-concavity of the n-th root of a sequence"],"author":[{"given":"Ernest X. W.","family":"Xia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Suzhou University of Science and Technology"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Zuo-Ru","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Hebei Normal University"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2022,12,12]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.21203\/rs.3.rs-2352868\/v1"},{"DOI":"10.2307\/2531282","title":["A Generalization of the Mantel-Haenszel Estimator of Partial Association for 2 x J x K Tables"],"author":[{"given":"Ruth M.","family":"Mickey","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Robert M.","family":"Elashoff","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[1985,9]]},"container-title":["Biometrics"],"type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":20,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2307\/2531282"},{"abstract":"<jats:p>The purpose of this article is to present a new sequence of numbers using the concept binomial coefficient. This new sequence is a generalization of Narayana\u2019s numbers. From this definition we will establish some properties, we will prove some identities and establish connections between this new sequence and the Catalan numbers. Finally, the generalized Narayana central numbers are defined and for some special cases, such as r = 1, 2, 3 and 4, identities involving the generalized Narayana centralnumbers and Catalan numbers are given and thus we establish a formula for the central Narayana numbers in terms of the Catalan numbers.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.34179\/revisem.v10i1.21294","type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["A NOTE ON GENERALIZED NARAYANA SEQUENCE"],"author":[{"given":"Adriana","family":"Wagner","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Andreia Cristina","family":"Ribeiro","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Irene","family":"Magalhaes Craveiro","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Tatiana","family":"Bertoldi Carlos","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"container-title":["Revista Sergipana de Matem\u00e1tica e Educa\u00e7\u00e3o Matem\u00e1tica"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,18]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.34179\/revisem.v10i1.21294"},{"DOI":"10.1006\/anbo.1999.0940","title":["Distribution of Lateral Root Primordia in Root Tips of Musa"],"author":[{"given":"X","family":"DRAYE","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"d